  <text>
    <body>
      <div type="transcription" xml:id="transcription_aad_0174" xml:lang="en">
          <div type="letter">
        <pb facs="https://iiif.acdh.oeaw.ac.at/aad/aad_00523/" ed="1r" type="sheet"/>
            <div type="letter_message" hand="#hand_black_gill">
              <opener>
                <dateline>  
                  <date>
                    <lb/>May 7, 1973
                  </date>
                </dateline>
                <salute>
                  <lb/>Dear <rs type="person" ref="#amp_person_1">Mr. Auden</rs>.
                </salute>
              </opener>
              <p>
                <lb/>Back from our Spring
                <lb/>break (spent mine lecturing
                <lb/>at <rs type="org" ref="#amp_organization_399">Stanford</rs>)<unclear>,</unclear> and eager to
                <lb/>resume our cabled
                <lb/>negotiations.
              </p>
              <p>
                <lb/>As it happens, <rs type="person" ref="#amp_person_598">Prof.
                <lb/>Gerald Lynch</rs>, vice-president
                <lb/>of <rs type="org" ref="#amp_organization_400">John Jay College</rs>, is in <rs type="place" ref="#amp_place_id_239">England</rs>
                <lb/>right now, and will be calling
                <lb/>you (probably already has)
                <lb/>to see whether he can't come
                <lb/>by to settle details with you
                <lb/>in person.
              </p>
              <p>
                <lb/>I do hope you can see
                <lb/><rs type="person" ref="#amp_person_598">him</rs>. We are all eager to
              </p>
            </div>
        <pb facs="https://iiif.acdh.oeaw.ac.at/aad/aad_00524/" ed="1v" type="sheet"/>
            <div>
              <ab hand="#hand_blue_unident_0174">
                <lb/>86
              </ab>
            </div>
            <div type="letter_message" hand="#hand_black_gill">
              <p>
                <lb/>have everything signed
                <lb/>and sealed so we can
                <lb/>begin to bask in the honor
                <lb/>you do us, and to savor
                <lb/>our delight.
              </p>
              <p>
                <lb/><rs type="person" ref="#amp_person_599">Prof. John Cammett</rs>, Dean
                <lb/>of Faculty, here, is sending
                <lb/>the formal letter of invitation
                <lb/>which should answer
                <lb/>whatever questions remain.
                <lb/>And I, who hosted the ARC
                <lb/>bon voyage party for you at <rs type="org" ref="#amp_organization_402">The
                <lb/>Players</rs> last year, will be
                <lb/>fatting a calf for you there
                <lb/>against the day of your return.
              </p>
              <closer>
                <salute>
                  <lb/>Cordially,
                </salute>
                <signed>
                  <lb/><rs type="person" ref="#amp_person_597">T<gap reason="illegible" quantity="1" unit="char"></gap>d Gill</rs>
                </signed>
              </closer>
            </div>
          </div>
      </div>
    </body>
